WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.540
- You have footprints
in all of the sciences,

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.940
so let's talk about the
universe a little bit.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.860
Is the universe, at the
lowest level, deterministic

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.370
or stochastic, in your
amateur philosophy view?

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.100
Put another way, does God play dice?

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.770
- We know it is stochastic, right?

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:20.603
Because--

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:22.130
- Today, today we think it is stochastic.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.130
- Yes, we think, because we have

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.080
the Heisenberg uncertainty principle,

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.683
and we have some
experiments to confirm that.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.920
- All we have is
experiments to confirm it.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.243
We don't understand why.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.470
- Why is already--

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:42.040
- You wrote a book about why. (laughs)

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.210
- Yeah, it's a puzzle.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.610
It's a puzzle that you have

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:50.073
the dice-flipping machine, or God,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.760
and the result of the flipping
propagated with a speed

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.260
faster than the speed of light. (laughs)

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.190
We can't explain it, okay.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:06.190
So, but it only governs
microscopic phenomena.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.530
- So you don't think of quantum mechanics

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.670
- as useful
- No.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.210
- For understanding the nature of reality.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.370
- No, it's diversionary.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:21.760
- So, in your thinking,
the world might as well

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.960
be deterministic.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.610
- The world is deterministic

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:29.760
and as far as the neuron
firing is concerned,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.743
it's deterministic to first approximation.

